body:
![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The 'artifactReceipt' function unconditionally calls 'sha256File(root, relPath)' even if the file does not exist. Since 'sha256File' does not have an existence check and directly calls 'fs.readFileSync', this will throw an 'ENOENT' error and crash the script when optional files are missing. In validation scripts, we should convert source-artifact path, read, or shape problems into stable validator warning/failure metadata instead of throwing raw parser or load failures. We should check if the file exists before attempting to calculate its SHA-256 hash.

```suggestion
function artifactReceipt(root, role, relPath, required = true) {
  const target = path.join(root, relPath);
  const exists = fs.existsSync(target);
  return {
    role,
    path: relPath,
    required,
    exists,
    sha256: exists ? sha256File(root, relPath) : null,
  };
}
```

